    "body": "Follow-up from #155 (PR #469), from the contributor's hands-on check.\n\n**Today:** with a Go home entry last in the program, the Fanuc post writes `G91 G28 Z0` / `G28 X0 Y0` for the entry, then `G90`, then the same pair again for the post's own end-of-program home before `M30`. The second home is a no-op on the machine, so this is harmless but redundant output.\n\n**Expected:** a trailing Go home entry (no posted op after it) merges with the post's end-of-program home, so it is written once. A Go home between operations stays as it is.\n\n**Done means:** a golden with a trailing Go home shows one home before `M30`. Mid-program homes are unchanged, and Suppress and \"Skip pauses and homes\" still apply.",
